        <briefdescription>
<para>Compute stress with time substepping and analytical tangent accumulation. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>response</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Constitutive response to be computed. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>tangents</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Algorithmic moduli to be computed. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>deformation</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Current deformation state. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>timeIncrement</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Time increment information.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
The deformation increment is divided into nSubsteps sub-increments. For each sub-increment, the base material&apos;s stress update is called, and the sensitivities are used to accumulate the overall tangent. </para>
